One final conceptual audit found the selector convention was still too arbitrary: “first 1 and its successor” was not structurally encoded by the instance. I’m replacing it with a genuine visible invariant—the lexicographically least address has exactly two 1-bits, and those two support coordinates define the quadratic product. This keeps the same 162-operation route but makes it inferable from the single instance. It requires one last full gate and oracle regeneration, which I’m doing rather than shipping a secret convention.
